From: Longwei Yang <19267252+Longwei-Yang@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 15:45:52 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] Safarium: vertical tabs sharing the Compact tab bar;
 overview fixes

Vertical tabs (Settings > Appearance > Tab position):
- The window drops its NSToolbar and the page runs to the top edge; the
  sidebar hosts the same AppKit tab bar view as horizontal mode, so
  address editing, hover cards, load progress, drag/reorder and tear-off
  are shared. Vertical rows are left-aligned (favicon where the hover
  close button appears) with concentric capsule corners.
- Sidebar controls are Liquid Glass buttons; downloads opens the native
  popover. Extension side panels can dock in the sidebar's lower half.
- Traffic lights follow AppKit's own metrics for Safarium windows; the
  toolbarless vertical layout uses a 52pt title bar (system sidebar
  apps' position).

Tab overview animation:
- The active card's selection ring animates in with the zoom instead of
  showing as a thick frame at full zoom.
- Card thumbnails no longer cross-fade, and the active card keeps the
  page snapshot taken on entry, removing doubled text on entry/exit.

Vertical-tab work is largely from the Codex thread; overview fixes were
verified frame by frame at 60fps.

Local checkpoint only; not intended for upstream.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
